    pmh: "COPD (GOLD Stage 3), Hypertension, Osteoporosis (from long-term steroid use)",
    medHx: "Tiotropium 18mcg inhaler daily (uses occasionally), Salbutamol MDI PRN, no ICS/LABA. Amlodipine 5mg daily.",
    allergies: "NKDA",
    pe: "Barrel-shaped chest, pursed-lip breathing, use of accessory muscles. Diffuse wheeze and prolonged expiration. Decreased breath sounds at bases. No peripheral oedema. JVP not elevated.",
