    carePlan: "Admit for IV antibiotics and intensive chest physiotherapy. Send sputum for culture and sensitivity. Start IV Ceftazidime 2g Q8H + Ciprofloxacin 750mg PO BID. Monitor sputum volume and purulence daily. Consider N-acetylcysteine 600mg BID as mucolytic. If frequent exacerbations (>3/year), consider long-term macrolide therapy (Azithromycin 250mg 3x/week).",
    dtps: "1. Acute infective exacerbation of bronchiectasis with Pseudomonas requiring targeted antibiotic therapy. 2. Chronic sputum production and impaired airway clearance requiring physiotherapy. 3. Risk of disease progression and lung function decline with each exacerbation.",
